1
00:00:14,933 --> 00:00:16,067
Oh my god!

2
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:18,467
Aah! We're about to kiss!

3
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:19,700
Huh?

4
00:00:19,833 --> 00:00:20,833
Bestie?

5
00:00:20,967 --> 00:00:22,700
Girl, wake up!

6
00:00:24,567 --> 00:00:25,733
You're acting weird.

7
00:00:25,867 --> 00:00:28,600
You're starting to
dream about him.

8
00:00:28,733 --> 00:00:30,000
So what's the meaning of this?

9
00:00:30,133 --> 00:00:31,967
Nadia, I've found her.

10
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:34,567
She's kind, but not gentle.

11
00:00:34,733 --> 00:00:35,833
She's Princess Janine.

12
00:00:35,967 --> 00:00:37,633
Princess Janine?

13
00:00:37,767 --> 00:00:38,733
Nadia?

14
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:40,667
Nadia.

15
00:00:41,867 --> 00:00:43,400
You're awake!

16
00:00:44,167 --> 00:00:46,033
Thank goodness.

17
00:00:46,167 --> 00:00:48,367
Treb, I'm so happy for you!

18
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:50,367
And because Grandma Nadia
is finally awake,

19
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:52,833
you can finally
make it up to her.

20
00:00:52,967 --> 00:00:54,867
Did you tell
Grandma Nadia about me?

21
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:56,567
What?

22
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:58,033
Oh, about that.

23
00:00:59,267 --> 00:01:03,300
Nadia used to love
my stories about a princess.

24
00:01:03,433 --> 00:01:04,467
Me?

25
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:05,700
A princess?

26
00:01:05,833 --> 00:01:07,167
Huh?

27
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:08,867
Well, yeah. It suits you.

28
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:13,733
A princess who's rough
around the edges.

29
00:01:15,867 --> 00:01:18,133
You're so annoying!

30
00:01:18,267 --> 00:01:21,900
You know, it's because
of my sweet voice

31
00:01:22,033 --> 00:01:23,767
that Grandma Nadia woke up.

32
00:01:24,933 --> 00:01:27,533
Yes. That's definitely
possible.

33
00:01:37,267 --> 00:01:40,100
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

34
00:01:40,233 --> 00:01:43,367
[PHONE CHIMES]

35
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:48,367
- "Where are they?"
- "Why haven't they posted?"

36
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:50,800
[BEEPING]

37
00:01:50,933 --> 00:01:57,767
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

38
00:02:08,267 --> 00:02:11,467
I hope Nadia and I can
still fix things between us.

39
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:12,733
Yes!

40
00:02:12,867 --> 00:02:14,200
So you can...

41
00:02:16,700 --> 00:02:18,033
...finally move on.

42
00:02:18,167 --> 00:02:25,167
["MULTO" BY
HEALY AFTER DARK PLAYING]

43
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:39,300
[JAJA] I'll call Bert!

44
00:02:40,067 --> 00:02:42,300
Princess Janine.

45
00:02:52,267 --> 00:02:54,500
[TONY] We've been friends
for five decades now.

46
00:02:54,633 --> 00:02:56,900
But I haven't seen you
like this before.

47
00:02:57,033 --> 00:02:59,700
You put in so much effort
just to make her happy.

48
00:02:59,833 --> 00:03:06,700
["MULTO" CONTINUES]

49
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:13,667
[EMMA] Girl, this is
something else.

50
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:16,200
Have you fallen in love
with him already?

51
00:03:20,867 --> 00:03:27,700
["MULTO" CONTINUES]

52
00:03:30,733 --> 00:03:33,933
[EMMA] You're giddy because
you feel something for him.

53
00:03:34,067 --> 00:03:35,733
But that isn't love.

54
00:03:35,867 --> 00:03:37,200
Not yet, at least.

55
00:03:37,333 --> 00:03:38,933
Girl, you might
actually fall for him.

56
00:03:39,067 --> 00:03:40,933
You know how this will end.

57
00:03:41,067 --> 00:03:47,933
["MULTO" CONTINUES]

58
00:03:55,500 --> 00:04:02,567
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

59
00:04:36,633 --> 00:04:37,500
Okay.

60
00:04:38,333 --> 00:04:40,500
Girl, let's go!

61
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:43,900
Girl, aren't you ready?!

62
00:04:44,033 --> 00:04:45,600
It's noon already!

63
00:04:46,833 --> 00:04:50,400
Oh, let's give the siblings
some time alone.

64
00:04:50,533 --> 00:04:53,300
[EMMA] But how? They can't
communicate with each other.

65
00:04:53,433 --> 00:04:56,233
They need a translator,
and that's you, correct?

66
00:04:56,367 --> 00:04:59,367
Mm. You expect Treb
to just stare at her?

67
00:04:59,500 --> 00:05:02,667
-[TONY] Yoo-hoo! Can we come in?
- [QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

68
00:05:02,833 --> 00:05:04,233
They're here.

69
00:05:04,367 --> 00:05:05,533
Okay.

70
00:05:07,233 --> 00:05:08,733
Treb.

71
00:05:08,867 --> 00:05:10,133
Where's Tony?

72
00:05:10,267 --> 00:05:11,567
- Boo!
- Oh!

73
00:05:11,700 --> 00:05:14,733
What's your problem?
Are you crazy?!

74
00:05:14,867 --> 00:05:16,367
What do you mean?

75
00:05:16,500 --> 00:05:18,900
Who's truly crazy here?

76
00:05:19,033 --> 00:05:21,033
[LAUGHS]

77
00:05:21,167 --> 00:05:23,533
Uh, so...

78
00:05:24,233 --> 00:05:25,333
How's Grandma doing?

79
00:05:25,467 --> 00:05:26,700
[DOOR CLOSES]

80
00:05:26,833 --> 00:05:28,700
She's fine.

81
00:05:28,833 --> 00:05:30,000
She's talkative now.

82
00:05:30,133 --> 00:05:32,433
It's like she was
never in a coma.

83
00:05:32,567 --> 00:05:35,000
She laughs with Bert a lot.

84
00:05:35,167 --> 00:05:36,500
Love it!

85
00:05:36,633 --> 00:05:38,233
That's good news,
right, bestie?

86
00:05:38,367 --> 00:05:41,100
Good news. Good news.
[CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

87
00:05:41,233 --> 00:05:43,533
That's why we've come
to pick you up.

88
00:05:43,667 --> 00:05:47,467
- Oh, you guys shouldn't have.
- [COUGHS]

89
00:05:48,900 --> 00:05:51,933
[COUGHING]

90
00:05:52,067 --> 00:05:55,233
- Jaja.
- [COUGHING]

91
00:05:55,367 --> 00:05:57,467
- Are you all right?
- Um...

92
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:00,567
I don't feel well today.

93
00:06:00,700 --> 00:06:04,067
[JAJA CONTINUES COUGHING]

94
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:07,300
Grandma might catch this cough.

95
00:06:07,467 --> 00:06:09,133
Oh, okay. Emma can just--

96
00:06:09,267 --> 00:06:11,300
- [COUGHING INTENSIFIES]
- I can go.

97
00:06:11,433 --> 00:06:14,833
[COUGHING CONTINUES]

98
00:06:14,967 --> 00:06:16,667
Bestie is asymptomatic.

99
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:18,033
As you know...

100
00:06:18,167 --> 00:06:20,467
[COUGHS]

101
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:23,667
You know she stays with me.

102
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:26,500
She could still be carrying
the virus. [COUGHS]

103
00:06:26,633 --> 00:06:29,133
We just don't know it.

104
00:06:29,267 --> 00:06:31,633
You sound like the MetroCom.

105
00:06:31,767 --> 00:06:33,333
You keep firing!
[IMITATES GUNFIRE]

106
00:06:33,467 --> 00:06:36,567
[EMMA] Wait.
MetroCom? What's that?

107
00:06:36,700 --> 00:06:39,667
[TONY] MetroCom.
They're the police. Cops.

108
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:42,600
I think you should
sit down, Jaja.

109
00:06:42,767 --> 00:06:45,100
- Take a break.
- Thank you.

110
00:06:45,233 --> 00:06:47,300
Uh, Emma.

111
00:06:47,433 --> 00:06:50,900
Would you mind boiling
some oregano leaves?

112
00:06:51,733 --> 00:06:53,700
And maybe squeeze
some limes too.

113
00:06:55,100 --> 00:06:57,467
- Thank you.
- Uh, thanks for the concern,

114
00:06:57,600 --> 00:07:00,000
but I have some medicine.

115
00:07:00,133 --> 00:07:02,467
[JAJA COUGHS, CLEARS THROAT]

116
00:07:07,300 --> 00:07:09,267
I wish I could
take care of you.

117
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:16,467
[ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]

118
00:07:24,867 --> 00:07:27,233
What are you talking about?

119
00:07:27,367 --> 00:07:29,667
[CLEARS THROAT]

120
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:31,033
I'm fine.

121
00:07:31,167 --> 00:07:32,933
I think I'll survive.

122
00:07:33,067 --> 00:07:37,800
[COUGHS]

123
00:07:37,933 --> 00:07:39,367
- Bestie?
- Hmm?

124
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:43,067
I need some water.
[CONTINUES COUGHING]

125
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:44,700
Girl, it's right
in front of you.

126
00:07:44,833 --> 00:07:46,567
It's been there the whole time.

127
00:07:46,700 --> 00:07:49,400
Mm-hmm. I know.
[CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

128
00:07:49,567 --> 00:07:56,600
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

129
00:08:07,133 --> 00:08:13,967
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

130
00:08:21,333 --> 00:08:23,233
[ENGINE REVS]

131
00:08:23,367 --> 00:08:25,433
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING
OVER SPEAKERS]

132
00:08:25,567 --> 00:08:28,233
One, two, three.

133
00:08:28,367 --> 00:08:30,067
I'll stay here, okay?

134
00:08:30,200 --> 00:08:31,600
I'll keep you company.

135
00:08:34,067 --> 00:08:35,667
It's okay, Treb.

136
00:08:35,800 --> 00:08:38,433
Grandma needs you. [COUGHS]

137
00:08:38,567 --> 00:08:40,600
Grandma needs you
more than I do.

138
00:08:41,467 --> 00:08:43,267
- [JAJA COUGHS]
- She's fine now.

139
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:45,600
Her condition has improved.

140
00:08:45,733 --> 00:08:47,900
I'll just stay here
and keep an eye on you.

141
00:08:49,833 --> 00:08:52,400
It's okay, Treb, I promise.

142
00:08:52,533 --> 00:08:56,233
Uh, but if you want
to stay here...

143
00:08:57,533 --> 00:08:59,067
...that's okay, too.

144
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:01,567
[CLEARS THROAT]

145
00:09:01,700 --> 00:09:03,333
I keep looking for your voice.

146
00:09:03,467 --> 00:09:05,100
[THUDS] Really?

147
00:09:06,533 --> 00:09:08,667
Uh, yes.

148
00:09:08,800 --> 00:09:10,900
- It's soothing.
- Oh.

149
00:09:12,867 --> 00:09:15,767
And Nadia keeps looking
for your voice.

150
00:09:15,900 --> 00:09:18,733
She keeps talking about
hearing a woman's voice.

151
00:09:18,867 --> 00:09:21,700
So we decided to
fetch you and Emma.

152
00:09:21,833 --> 00:09:24,900
I hope you get
to talk to her already.

153
00:09:25,033 --> 00:09:27,033
That way, I can communicate
with my sister.

154
00:09:27,167 --> 00:09:30,100
Is that so? Why didn't you
tell me right away?

155
00:09:31,167 --> 00:09:34,267
Because I was worried
about your cough.

156
00:09:34,400 --> 00:09:36,133
I'm going to get dressed now.

157
00:09:36,267 --> 00:09:38,167
- We'll go there now.
- Wow! [EMMA CLAPS]

158
00:09:38,300 --> 00:09:41,333
It's a miracle!
Your cough is gone already?

159
00:09:41,467 --> 00:09:46,333
You sounded like Susan Africa
with all your coughing earlier.

160
00:09:46,467 --> 00:09:49,200
Praise the Lord!
It's a miracle!

161
00:09:49,333 --> 00:09:51,767
Praise the Lord
for I am healed!

162
00:09:51,900 --> 00:09:52,767
Amen.

163
00:09:52,900 --> 00:09:54,833
You can cure coughs
instantly now?

164
00:09:54,967 --> 00:09:56,767
- That's awesome!
- Mm-hmm.

165
00:10:02,433 --> 00:10:05,233
You know, you guys
should go ahead.

166
00:10:05,367 --> 00:10:07,233
Jaja and I will follow, okay?

167
00:10:07,367 --> 00:10:08,900
She just needs to rest a bit,

168
00:10:09,033 --> 00:10:12,033
but I think she'll be
better soon.

169
00:10:12,167 --> 00:10:13,533
Up to you.

170
00:10:13,667 --> 00:10:15,067
- Yes.
- Okay.

171
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:16,500
Thank you. Bye, guys.

172
00:10:16,633 --> 00:10:17,733
Are we leaving?

173
00:10:17,867 --> 00:10:20,300
I was about to
perfect that dance.

174
00:10:20,433 --> 00:10:23,567
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

175
00:10:23,700 --> 00:10:25,167
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

176
00:10:27,233 --> 00:10:28,267
[DOOR CLOSES]

177
00:10:31,900 --> 00:10:38,800
[COUGHS]

178
00:10:41,500 --> 00:10:43,633
You said you weren't
in love with him.

179
00:10:43,767 --> 00:10:46,267
- I thought so too, bestie.
- Bestie...

180
00:10:46,400 --> 00:10:48,733
He's just different from Vhal.

181
00:10:49,933 --> 00:10:53,800
[SIGHS] I was all over the place
when I was with Vhal.

182
00:10:54,567 --> 00:10:56,700
I kept chasing him.

183
00:10:56,833 --> 00:11:00,700
But with Wilberto,
it's different.

184
00:11:02,433 --> 00:11:04,067
[JAJA] It feels like...

185
00:11:04,900 --> 00:11:06,733
...I don't need to
chase after him.

186
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:11,167
I feel relaxed and chill.

187
00:11:11,333 --> 00:11:12,567
[JAJA] That's how I feel.

188
00:11:12,700 --> 00:11:14,400
Oh, come on.

189
00:11:14,533 --> 00:11:15,900
Bestie, it's not my fault

190
00:11:16,033 --> 00:11:18,067
that I have feelings
for a ghost.

191
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:22,100
- Tsk.
- I've moved on from Vhal.

192
00:11:22,233 --> 00:11:24,233
[SIGHS] Girl.

193
00:11:24,367 --> 00:11:26,867
We opened your third eye,
not your heart.

194
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:30,400
Can't you close your heart?
It's not good for you. Tsk.

195
00:11:30,533 --> 00:11:32,533
I don't want him to go.

196
00:11:32,667 --> 00:11:34,800
When he fixes things
with Grandma Nadia,

197
00:11:34,933 --> 00:11:36,967
we won't see
each other again, bestie.

198
00:11:39,533 --> 00:11:41,167
Oh.

199
00:11:41,300 --> 00:11:45,900
So that's why you were
pretending to have a cough.

200
00:11:46,067 --> 00:11:48,500
It's just a delaying tactic.

201
00:11:48,633 --> 00:11:50,167
But I promised him

202
00:11:50,300 --> 00:11:52,933
that I would help him
and Grandma Nadia.

203
00:11:54,033 --> 00:11:57,667
[SIGHS] And I don't plan on
breaking that promise.

204
00:11:59,100 --> 00:12:03,000
When that happens,
I'll be happy for them.

205
00:12:05,933 --> 00:12:08,767
[JAJA] I'll go get ready.
They might be waiting for us.

206
00:12:10,567 --> 00:12:17,100
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

207
00:12:25,667 --> 00:12:27,300
Good afternoon.

208
00:12:28,867 --> 00:12:31,033
That's the voice I heard.

209
00:12:33,300 --> 00:12:35,400
I'm sorry I let her in--

210
00:12:37,367 --> 00:12:38,833
I want to get to know her.

211
00:12:38,967 --> 00:12:40,433
Hello, Grandma.

212
00:12:46,333 --> 00:12:49,267
You can call me Jaja.

213
00:12:49,433 --> 00:12:52,267
My real name is Janine.

214
00:12:52,400 --> 00:12:54,267
Princess Janine.

215
00:12:58,433 --> 00:13:01,767
I also heard a man's voice.

216
00:13:01,900 --> 00:13:04,033
Was that my brother, Wilberto?

217
00:13:10,933 --> 00:13:13,733
It's been ages since
we last saw each other.

218
00:13:13,867 --> 00:13:19,933
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

219
00:13:20,067 --> 00:13:23,400
Many people have tried
connecting my brother and I.

220
00:13:25,033 --> 00:13:28,400
[LABORED BREATHING]

221
00:13:28,533 --> 00:13:33,300
Maybe it's better he never
saw where I ended up.

222
00:13:37,933 --> 00:13:40,900
Since we lost our parents...

223
00:13:42,067 --> 00:13:43,800
[NADIA]
...he changed.

224
00:13:46,300 --> 00:13:48,133
Nadia.

225
00:13:48,267 --> 00:13:51,033
Stay here, okay?
Take care of yourself.

226
00:13:51,167 --> 00:13:53,733
Can I come with you, Wilberto?

227
00:13:53,867 --> 00:13:55,433
You can't.

228
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:59,800
But, Wilberto, I don't
want to be alone.

229
00:13:59,933 --> 00:14:04,367
Can you tell me the story
about the princess?

230
00:14:04,500 --> 00:14:05,700
It's getting dark.

231
00:14:05,833 --> 00:14:07,867
I need to find us some food.

232
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:10,100
I'll help you.

233
00:14:10,233 --> 00:14:12,167
[CLICKS TONGUE]
Cut it out, Nadia .

234
00:14:13,933 --> 00:14:15,567
Stop being a burden.

235
00:14:18,267 --> 00:14:20,767
[NADIA]
He lost his temper often.

236
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:22,467
He became very strict.

237
00:14:24,067 --> 00:14:27,200
I felt like he loved our country
more than he loved me.

238
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:35,933
Just stay here, okay?

239
00:14:36,067 --> 00:14:37,933
Don't go out.

240
00:14:38,067 --> 00:14:40,867
I left you some food.

241
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:44,900
I'm scared
you'll leave me, Wilberto.

242
00:14:49,167 --> 00:14:52,600
I promise
I'll come back for you.

243
00:14:54,933 --> 00:14:57,533
- [SMOOCHES]
- [SNIFFLES]

244
00:14:57,667 --> 00:14:59,700
I'll be back.

245
00:14:59,833 --> 00:15:06,900
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

246
00:15:09,900 --> 00:15:16,933
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

247
00:15:19,867 --> 00:15:26,933
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

248
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:32,733
WIlberto?

249
00:15:32,867 --> 00:15:39,933
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

250
00:15:43,033 --> 00:15:45,200
Wilberto?

251
00:15:49,900 --> 00:15:53,767
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

252
00:15:53,900 --> 00:15:56,200
Wilberto?

253
00:15:58,400 --> 00:16:02,333
[NADIA]
I waited, and I waited...

254
00:16:02,467 --> 00:16:05,600
Until the days
turned into weeks.

255
00:16:05,733 --> 00:16:08,900
[COUGHING]

256
00:16:10,733 --> 00:16:16,167
[COUGHING]

257
00:16:16,300 --> 00:16:21,600
I felt like he
abandoned me because...

258
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:26,567
Because I was a burden to him.

259
00:16:26,700 --> 00:16:31,567
I told myself that I was
going to fight for my life.

260
00:16:31,700 --> 00:16:34,433
I am not a burden.

261
00:16:39,367 --> 00:16:43,200
I never became
a burden to anyone.

262
00:16:44,867 --> 00:16:47,067
I didn't mean to do that.

263
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:49,733
I was angry back then.

264
00:16:49,867 --> 00:16:54,267
I didn't realize that you were
hurt by my actions and words.

265
00:16:59,567 --> 00:17:01,967
He says that
he didn't mean to do that.

266
00:17:02,100 --> 00:17:04,767
He was just angry back then.

267
00:17:04,900 --> 00:17:08,433
That's why he said
those harsh words.

268
00:17:08,567 --> 00:17:11,567
He was guilty.

269
00:17:11,700 --> 00:17:14,600
Aren't you a translator?

270
00:17:14,767 --> 00:17:17,667
Why are you defending him?

271
00:17:20,600 --> 00:17:23,900
I experienced something
similar to you, Grandma.

272
00:17:24,033 --> 00:17:26,967
I have also been left behind
and abandoned.

273
00:17:27,100 --> 00:17:31,133
Mm? Then shouldn't we
be on the same side?

274
00:17:31,267 --> 00:17:34,767
Grandma, what differs
in our situations is that...

275
00:17:34,900 --> 00:17:39,800
The person who
left you is... here now.

276
00:17:39,933 --> 00:17:47,000
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

277
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:50,567
Tell her that
I won't give up on her.

278
00:17:50,700 --> 00:17:54,200
He says that he won't give up
until he earns your forgiveness.

279
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:59,800
I have very little time left
in this world.

280
00:17:59,933 --> 00:18:06,533
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

281
00:18:06,667 --> 00:18:09,967
He says he has very
little time left in this world.

282
00:18:10,100 --> 00:18:12,667
Are we going to waste
that time left?

283
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:22,667
Let's do what we have to do,
and say what we have to say.

284
00:18:26,533 --> 00:18:28,800
I love you.

285
00:18:28,933 --> 00:18:35,767
[ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]

286
00:18:38,933 --> 00:18:42,667
[ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]

287
00:18:42,800 --> 00:18:44,633
You love them.

288
00:18:44,767 --> 00:18:46,833
Huh? Uh... Who?

289
00:18:46,967 --> 00:18:48,767
- You.
- Her.

290
00:18:50,633 --> 00:18:53,100
Uh... Yes, Grandma.

291
00:18:53,233 --> 00:18:56,433
He loves you so much.

292
00:19:00,733 --> 00:19:06,200
He is here to ask
for your forgiveness.

293
00:19:10,500 --> 00:19:13,833
I just wanted to protect you,
so I joined the guerrillas.

294
00:19:18,033 --> 00:19:21,167
But I didn't know that I would
never be able to come back.

295
00:19:23,267 --> 00:19:25,867
He wanted to protect you,

296
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:30,133
that's why he joined
the guerrillas.

297
00:19:30,300 --> 00:19:32,533
And that's where he was killed.

298
00:19:34,333 --> 00:19:37,700
That's why he couldn't
come back to you.

299
00:19:44,400 --> 00:19:48,167
Other people have told me
about Wilberto's presence,

300
00:19:48,300 --> 00:19:51,133
but I always ignored it.

301
00:19:52,800 --> 00:19:58,600
I had to almost die
before I listened to him.

302
00:20:00,867 --> 00:20:03,000
It's all right, Grandma.

303
00:20:03,167 --> 00:20:05,433
You were hurt.

304
00:20:05,567 --> 00:20:08,767
What matters
is that you're here.

305
00:20:08,900 --> 00:20:14,000
[SOBBING]

306
00:20:14,133 --> 00:20:16,800
Wilberto...

307
00:20:20,533 --> 00:20:25,833
[SNIFFLES] Wilberto, I don't
want us angry at each other.

308
00:20:29,033 --> 00:20:33,833
Wilberto, I forgive you.

309
00:20:33,967 --> 00:20:40,767
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

310
00:20:55,967 --> 00:21:02,767
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

311
00:21:16,967 --> 00:21:23,800
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

312
00:21:25,667 --> 00:21:31,367
- [VEHICLES RUMBLING]
- [HORNS HONKING]

313
00:21:31,500 --> 00:21:36,100
I know that he's going
to leave soon, bestie, but...

314
00:21:36,233 --> 00:21:40,133
It's still too painful for me.

315
00:21:40,267 --> 00:21:43,000
Why am I so weak?

316
00:21:48,133 --> 00:21:50,300
What's wrong?

317
00:21:53,800 --> 00:21:59,567
["PAUWI NA AKO"
BY GAB PLAYING]

318
00:21:59,700 --> 00:22:01,833
Baby!

319
00:22:01,967 --> 00:22:08,800
["PAUWI NA AKO" CONTINUES]

320
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:30,833
["PAUWI NA AKO" CONTINUES]

321
00:22:35,667 --> 00:22:38,033
So, are you excited
to enter heaven?

322
00:22:40,033 --> 00:22:41,433
Bro?

323
00:22:41,567 --> 00:22:43,300
Don't leave yet.

324
00:22:43,433 --> 00:22:45,967
- What?
- Don't go...

325
00:22:46,100 --> 00:22:47,467
I'll be right here, Jaja.

326
00:22:47,600 --> 00:22:50,900
- Vhal...
- Vhal?!

327
00:22:51,067 --> 00:22:52,300
What's this guy doing here?

328
00:22:52,433 --> 00:22:53,633
Oh, wow...

329
00:22:53,767 --> 00:22:55,367
I dare you to hurt Jaja again.

330
00:22:55,500 --> 00:22:56,933
Bro, he's getting scared.

331
00:22:57,067 --> 00:23:00,567
Come on, let's go.
He's about to bolt, man.

332
00:23:00,700 --> 00:23:02,133
Just leave her alone!

333
00:23:02,267 --> 00:23:03,500
Tell me you want
to get back with him.

334
00:23:03,633 --> 00:23:05,233
- Jaja.
- Come out here.

335
00:23:05,367 --> 00:23:08,300
Stop it!

336
00:23:08,433 --> 00:23:10,767
Could you two stop this?!

337
00:23:10,900 --> 00:23:14,567
Can you please not make this
any more complicated?!

338
00:23:14,700 --> 00:23:16,800
Jaja...

339
00:23:16,933 --> 00:23:21,733
[ELECTRICITY SPARKING]

340
00:23:28,733 --> 00:23:30,367
Jaja!
